    "corrects_earlier_reading": "An earlier reading recommended promoting step 2000 on the basis of top-3 family accuracy (atom_restate 0.208->0.528) and mean selected-mark probability (0.032->0.119). Both are ranking/confidence statistics and BOTH improve while canonical-successor LIKELIHOOD degrades: the model grows more confident on easy marks and much worse on the tail. Per-family canonical NLL shows step500 best on 6/9 families including EVERY lower-frequency family (atom_restate 7.559->8.333, bond_reorder 4.313->5.353, bond_reroute 8.105->8.397, ring_system_delete 3.619->4.424, ring_system_restate 4.247->5.230 across 500->2000). The frozen rule forbidding top-3 as the primary metric caught this.",
