    "open_issue": "\"Production-weighted\" requires the PRODUCTION family mix (manifest corruption 0.55 / mmp 0.45). The MMP pool lives on the Modal volume, so the local eval set approximates it. Ranking is mix-dependent between step500 and step1500 (never step2000), so the production mix must be used for the final selection on the corrected run.",
    "promote_step2000": false,
    "reason": "Step 2000 is NOT best on the primary canonical-successor NLL under ANY family weighting tested (my eval-set mix, the trainer validation mix, uniform), and it is also WORSE on family-mass calibration (TV 0.518 vs 0.359 at step500). The protocol condition for promotion -- best on canonical-successor NLL, or statistically tied while superior on balanced-family recovery and calibration -- fails on both clauses.",
